# Model Routing Strategy

**Default: use the Cursor Pro premium / advanced model** for all work in this project.

Use the **free model only** in these two cases:

## 1. GitHub pull / push (free model)

When the task is **only** (or primarily) syncing with GitHub via Git:

- `git pull`, `git fetch`, `git push`
- `git push -u origin …`
- Pre-push steps that exist solely to support push (e.g. `git status`, `git add`, `git commit` immediately before push when the user asked to push)

Response prefix (optional, one line):

> **Model**: Free model is sufficient (Git sync).

Then execute the Git workflow.

**Not free by default:** branch design, merge conflict resolution, PR description writing, code review, rebase strategy, or multi-step refactors that happen to include a push at the end — use **Pro premium**.

## 2. User explicitly requests free model (free model)

If the user clearly asks to use the free model (e.g. “使用免费模型”, “use free model”), honor that for the current task.

Response prefix (optional, one line):

> **Model**: Using free model as requested.

## Everything else (Pro premium)

Use **Pro premium / advanced model** without suggesting a switch, including:

- Architecture, multi-file features, complex bugs, algorithms, security review
- UI/UX design and implementation (Lite/Pro)
- Planning, debugging, tests, documentation
- Simple Q&A, typos, or small edits — still Pro unless case 1 or 2 applies

Do **not** default to the free model for “simple” tasks; only cases 1 and 2 above.

